SUMMARY:○ OPTIONAL easy spin 45-60 min
DESCRIPTION:OPTIONAL easy spin 45-60 min - Sunday is now a REST day by de
 fault. Take the ride only if you feel good and Monday's run is easy. Wit
 h a quality session on Monday you need this rest more than you need the 
 ride.\n\nWeek 9 of 17 - Build\nGUT TRAINING STARTS. Target 60-80 g carb/
 h by week 14\, from 40-50 now\, +10 g every two weeks. No drop bags and 
 no crew at Madeira - only ~2 checkpoints\, ~10 km apart - so you carry 4
 00-500 g of carbohydrate yourself. Rehearse the weight and the stowage\,
  not just the products. INTENSITY STARTS THIS WEEK\, on flat ground: Thu
 rsday's vertical stays STEADY because Hyrox is 8 x 1 km flat and stair f
 itness does not transfer. Target distribution is 80-85% easy\, 15-20% ha
 rd. ORDER CHANGED 31 Aug - threshold Mon -> Tue\, legs Tue -> Wed\, easy
  run + push Wed -> Mon. Reason is measurement\, not fatigue: resting HR 
 was 55 against a 50-52 baseline and HRV 78 against an 89 weekly average\
 , which distorts the HR-work relationship in both directions. This is th
 e first structured interval session of the block and its job is to estab
 lish what threshold feels like - a reference set on a distorted day gets
  trained off for weeks. Load is unchanged: three runs\, two gym sessions
 \, one vertical\, one rest day\, Friday still free. Legs on Wednesday ke
 eps 72 h before the long day\, the outer edge of the 48-72 h rule. Push 
 stays paired with the easy run\, pull with the vertical. STOPPING RULE: 
 the threshold session happens Tuesday regardless of readiness unless sle
 ep is under 6 h or HRV drops below 70.\n63 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
