BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w10-s7-benchmark@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260831T094658Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260908
SUMMARY:5 KM TIME TRIAL (5 km)
DESCRIPTION:5 KM TIME TRIAL - the number this whole plan has been missing
 . Warm up 10-15 min easy + 4-6 x 20 s strides + 3-4 min rest. Then 5 km 
 flat\, hard as you can SUSTAIN. Go out at 5:15/km and hold\, check in at
  2 km\, kick from 4 km. Do NOT start at 4:40 - a blown TT gives an unusa
 ble number. Flat\, no lights\, no turns: Vondelpark outer loop or the Am
 stel. Auto-lap every 1 km. Down week with Sunday rest behind you.\n\nWee
 k 10 of 17 - Build\nDOWN WEEK - recover\, do not add volume.\nCutback. D
 eliberate\, and the reason matters: in trail runners\, injury weeks were
  preceded by load DROPPING 16-24% then rebounding 15-37%. Yo-yo loading\
 , not absolute load\, is what precedes injury. This dip is planned and t
 he rebound is controlled.\n55 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w11-s0-cycling@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260831T094658Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260913
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260914
SUMMARY:○ OPTIONAL easy spin 45-60 min
DESCRIPTION:OPTIONAL easy spin 45-60 min - Sunday is now a REST day by de
 fault. Take the ride only if you feel good and Monday's run is easy. Wit
 h a quality session on Monday you need this rest more than you need the 
 ride.\n\nWeek 11 of 17 - Build\nTERRAIN WEEKEND #1 of 2 - Posbank/Veluwe
 zoom\, ~1h15 by car\, ~EUR 30 of petrol. Hard-surface descents\, 90-110 
 m climbs. Twenty reps is 1\,800 m of real ascent AND descent. One day th
 ere beats ten stairwell sessions\, because sand is compliant and actuall
 y REDUCES muscle damage relative to firm ground. Madeira is rock and sto
 ne steps.\n49 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
