END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w11-s3-legs@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260831T094658Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:◆ Legs ONLY\, no upper
DESCRIPTION:Legs ONLY\, no upper - heavy eccentric. Three quad lifts doin
 g three different jobs: HEAVY BILATERAL trap-bar deadlift 4 x 4-6 at 85 
 kg (18 Aug: 75x6x3 with 4+ reps in reserve\, so 1RM is nearer 100 - auto
 regulate to 2 REPS IN RESERVE and add 5 kg when the last set still feels
  easy)\, LOADED UNILATERAL Bulgarian split squat 3 x 8/leg with dumbbell
 s\, and TEMPO ECCENTRIC step-downs 3 x 8-10/leg with 3-4 s lowering. The
 n Nordics 3 x 5 and single-leg calf raises. Never to failure. 48-72 h be
 fore the long day. On a -15% descent hip drop is 23.7 mm vs 7.6 mm uphil
 l (very large effect)\, so descending is a frontal-plane hip problem and
  not only a quad problem - loaded Bulgarians carry that demand\, which i
 s why standalone side planks and cable abduction came out. HYROX SLED TE
 CHNIQUE at the end\, 8-10 x 12.5 m at 50-65% load (~100 kg)\, 60-90 s re
 st. TECHNIQUE ONLY\, never to fatigue. Forearms hooked on the posts\, 30
 -45 deg lean\, short choppy steps 20-30 cm at 3-4 per second\, and never
  let the sled stop. Sled push is PURELY CONCENTRIC\, so it costs your de
 scent block nothing - which is why it is the one Hyrox station you can t
 rain now. At 56 kg you need 1.03x bodyweight of horizontal force to brea
 k a stationary sled versus 0.81x to keep one rolling\, so learning not t
 o stop is worth more to you than to anyone heavier. About 8 minutes.\n\n
 Week 11 of 17 - Build\nTERRAIN WEEKEND #1 of 2 - Posbank/Veluwezoom\, ~1
 h15 by car\, ~EUR 30 of petrol. Hard-surface descents\, 90-110 m climbs.
  Twenty reps is 1\,800 m of real ascent AND descent. One day there beats
  ten stairwell sessions\, because sand is compliant and actually REDUCES
  muscle damage relative to firm ground. Madeira is rock and stone steps.
 \n47 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w11-s4-vertical@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260831T094658Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260917
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260918
SUMMARY:▲ VERTICAL 70 min STEADY
DESCRIPTION:VERTICAL 70 min STEADY - stairwell\, your own building or a c
 ar park. ~19 x 15 floors\, about 840 m. Lift up\, WALK DOWN - the descen
 t is the point. NO INTERVALS: the hard session moved to Monday on flat g
 round\, because Hyrox is 8 x 1 km on the flat and stair fitness does not
  transfer to flat running economy. This is now climbing endurance for Ma
 deira - steady\, conversational\, just keep moving. Dutch stair pitch is
  30-33 deg\, inside the optimal climbing range.\n\nWeek 11 of 17 - Build
 \nTERRAIN WEEKEND #1 of 2 - Posbank/Veluwezoom\, ~1h15 by car\, ~EUR 30 
 of petrol. Hard-surface descents\, 90-110 m climbs. Twenty reps is 1\,80
 0 m of real ascent AND descent. One day there beats ten stairwell sessio
 ns\, because sand is compliant and actually REDUCES muscle damage relati
 ve to firm ground. Madeira is rock and stone steps.\n45 days to Ultra X 
 Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w11-s5-pull@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260831T094658Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260917
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260918
SUMMARY:Pull (upper)
DESCRIPTION:Pull (upper) - after the vertical session. HYROX SEEDING\, al
 l substitutions not additions: (1) WARM UP ON THE SKIERG OR ROWER\, 5-8 
 min\, technique only - hinge and drive the first third of the pull\, tha
 t is where 80% of ski power comes from. Replaces your normal warm-up\, c
 osts nothing. (2) SWAP one row variation for a HEAVY FARMERS CARRY\, 4 x
  40-60 m. Same pulling pattern\, direct Hyrox transfer. (3) Finish with 
 DEAD HANGS\, 3 x max. Baseline 20 Aug was 32/36/31 s\, so 90 s by Octobe
 r was never realistic: target 55-60 s by 1 Nov and 90 s by Hyrox in Janu
 ary. Grip takes 4-6 weeks to change and it is what limits the farmers ca
 rry. About 3 minutes total added to the session.\n\nWeek 11 of 17 - Buil
 d\nTERRAIN WEEKEND #1 of 2 - Posbank/Veluwezoom\, ~1h15 by car\, ~EUR 30
  of petrol. Hard-surface descents\, 90-110 m climbs. Twenty reps is 1\,8
 00 m of real ascent AND descent. One day there beats ten stairwell sessi
 ons\, because sand is compliant and actually REDUCES muscle damage relat
 ive to firm ground. Madeira is rock and stone steps.\n45 days to Ultra X
  Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w11-s6-long@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260831T094658Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260919
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260920
SUMMARY:▲ LONG DAY 2:35\, 900 m vert (17 km)
DESCRIPTION:LONG DAY 2:35\, 900 m vert - Posbank if possible\, descents o
 n hard surface DESCENT CUE: shorten the step\, 185-195 spm. Understridin
 g cut strength loss to -8.8% vs -15.5% at preferred step length - roughl
 y halved. Do NOT coach foot strike: the more anterior the strike\, the L
 ARGER the quad torque loss. Let the terrain dictate it.\n\nWeek 11 of 17
  - Build\nKeep HR under 158. Walk the climbs. Talk test.\nTERRAIN WEEKEN
 D #1 of 2 - Posbank/Veluwezoom\, ~1h15 by car\, ~EUR 30 of petrol. Hard-
 surface descents\, 90-110 m climbs. Twenty reps is 1\,800 m of real asce
 nt AND descent. One day there beats ten stairwell sessions\, because san
 d is compliant and actually REDUCES muscle damage relative to firm groun
 d. Madeira is rock and stone steps.\n43 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w11-s7-easy@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260831T094658Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260914
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260915
SUMMARY:VO2MAX 5 x 3 min HARD\, 2 min easy jog. Warm up…
DESCRIPTION:VO2MAX 5 x 3 min HARD\, 2 min easy jog. Warm up 10 min\, cool
  down 10 min. Harder than threshold - one word at a time\, HR 180-190. P
 ace off the week 10 TT: roughly your 5 km pace\, no faster. THIS IS NOW 
 YOUR ONLY HARD SESSION\, so run it properly. It is the single session th
 at most moves 5 km pace\, and 5 km pace is what your Hyrox runs are made
  of.\n\nWeek 11 of 17 - Build\nKeep HR under 158. Walk the climbs. Talk 
 test.\nTERRAIN WEEKEND #1 of 2 - Posbank/Veluwezoom\, ~1h15 by car\, ~EU
 R 30 of petrol. Hard-surface descents\, 90-110 m climbs. Twenty reps is 
 1\,800 m of real ascent AND descent. One day there beats ten stairwell s
 essions\, because sand is compliant and actually REDUCES muscle damage r
 elative to firm ground. Madeira is rock and stone steps.\n48 days to Ult
 ra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
