UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w12-s7-descent@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260831T094658Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260920
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260921
SUMMARY:▼ ZIG-ZAG AND WET-ROCK PRACTICE 45 min.…
DESCRIPTION:ZIG-ZAG AND WET-ROCK PRACTICE 45 min. Traversing at 60 deg to
  the fall line halves the gradient\, 28% -> 14%. Wet volcanic rock and w
 et wooden steps sit at friction 0.3-0.5 - barely enough to stand on a 28
 % slope\, let alone brake. In the wet\, zig-zagging and side-stepping ar
 e technique\, not cowardice.\n\nWeek 12 of 17 - Build\nBiggest vertical 
 week so far\, ~2\,000-2\,300 m. HR is now unreliable as a guide: in moun
 tain ultras heart rate FALLS ~34 bpm across the race while RPE rises fro
 m 4.3 to 6.9. Pace off knee-extensor RPE - how your quads feel - not the
  watch.\n42 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w12-s8-descent@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260831T094658Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260922
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260923
SUMMARY:▼ PRECONDITIONING DOWNHILL WALK
DESCRIPTION:PRECONDITIONING DOWNHILL WALK - 5 minutes\, 5.6 kg in the pac
 k\, walking DOWN stairs. Lift up\, walk down\, repeat for 5 min. ~110 m 
 of descent\, about 37 flights. One bout cuts strength loss 49%\, CK 47%\
 , soreness 66% a week later. Five minutes\, in your own building\, no tr
 avel.\n\nWeek 12 of 17 - Build\nBiggest vertical week so far\, ~2\,000-2
 \,300 m. HR is now unreliable as a guide: in mountain ultras heart rate 
 FALLS ~34 bpm across the race while RPE rises from 4.3 to 6.9. Pace off 
 knee-extensor RPE - how your quads feel - not the watch.\n40 days to Ult
 ra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w12-s9-easy@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260831T094658Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260921
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260922
SUMMARY:VO2MAX 5 x 3 min HARD\, 2 min jog. Same as last…
DESCRIPTION:VO2MAX 5 x 3 min HARD\, 2 min jog. Same as last week - repeat
  before you progress. If rep 5 falls apart you started rep 1 too fast\; 
 even splits beat a fast start every time.\n\nWeek 12 of 17 - Build\nKeep
  HR under 158. Walk the climbs. Talk test.\nBiggest vertical week so far
 \, ~2\,000-2\,300 m. HR is now unreliable as a guide: in mountain ultras
  heart rate FALLS ~34 bpm across the race while RPE rises from 4.3 to 6.
 9. Pace off knee-extensor RPE - how your quads feel - not the watch.\n41
  days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w13-s0-cycling@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260831T094658Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260927
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260928
SUMMARY:○ OPTIONAL easy spin 45-60 min
DESCRIPTION:OPTIONAL easy spin 45-60 min - Sunday is now a REST day by de
 fault. Take the ride only if you feel good and Monday's run is easy. Wit
 h a quality session on Monday you need this rest more than you need the 
 ride.\n\nWeek 13 of 17 - Build\nDOWN WEEK - recover\, do not add volume.
 \nCutback before the two biggest weeks. Eat. At 56 kg with ~50 kg FFM yo
 u need at least 2\,250 kcal before exercise is counted - peak-week days 
 run 4\,800-5\,000 kcal. Under-fuelling an 11-week ramp is the most likel
 y route to a stress fracture\, and your body mass must not trend down.\n
 35 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
