BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w14-s0-cycling@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260831T094658Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261004
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261005
SUMMARY:○ OPTIONAL easy spin 45-60 min
DESCRIPTION:OPTIONAL easy spin 45-60 min - Sunday is now a REST day by de
 fault. Take the ride only if you feel good and Monday's run is easy. Wit
 h a quality session on Monday you need this rest more than you need the 
 ride.\n\nWeek 14 of 17 - Peak\nTERRAIN WEEKEND #2 - POSBANK AGAIN\, not 
 the Ardennes. Roughly EUR 30 of petrol against EUR 200\, and twenty reps
  of a 90-110 m climb is 1\,800 m of ascent AND hard-surface descent - cl
 ose to the whole race. Sustained descending on firm ground is the one th
 ing stairs cannot replicate\, and it is what decides your day. POLES: bo
 ught 18-20 Sep\, so you have had three weeks on them by now. Use them th
 e whole session. They cut RPE 14-18% and measurably reduce muscle damage
  over a climb-and-descent day - but an inexperienced pole user in a fiel
 d study actually got SLOWER\, so the practice is the point. KIT-CHECK HA
 BIT STARTS HERE: every food item must be labelled with its calorie count
 \, and all disposable packaging must carry your bib number. Tape a strip
  on your gel flask reading contents and total kcal (e.g. '4x Upfront Gel
  PRO - 640 kcal'). Do it from this session on\, not at registration.\n28
  days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
