DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261013
SUMMARY:VO2MAX 4 x 3 min HARD\, 2 min jog. Cut back a rep (8 km)
DESCRIPTION:VO2MAX 4 x 3 min HARD\, 2 min jog. Cut back a rep - Saturday 
 is the peak long day\, 3:45-4:00 with 1\,600-1\,800 m of vert\, and Mond
 ay is five days clear of it so this is affordable. If your legs are stil
 l flat from last Saturday\, run 3 reps.\n\nWeek 15 of 17 - Peak\nKeep HR
  under 158. Walk the climbs. Talk test.\nPEAK WEEKEND - Sat 17 Oct\, 15 
 days out. This is the overload the taper is built on\; the evidence favo
 urs peaking 14-15 days out\, not five weeks. 3:45-4:00 and 1\,600-1\,800
  m: roughly 60-70% of race duration but 80-90% of race vertical. Vertica
 l specificity is the lever\, not duration.\n20 days to Ultra X Madeira 2
 5K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w16-s0-cycling@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260831T094658Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261018
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261019
SUMMARY:○ OPTIONAL easy spin 45-60 min
DESCRIPTION:OPTIONAL easy spin 45-60 min - Sunday is now a REST day by de
 fault. Take the ride only if you feel good and Monday's run is easy. Wit
 h a quality session on Monday you need this rest more than you need the 
 ride.\n\nWeek 16 of 17 - Taper\nTaper starts. Volume down 45-55%\, inten
 sity and frequency UNCHANGED - that combination is worth 2-3%\, about 7-
 11 minutes on a 6-hour race. NOTHING ECCENTRIC AFTER 21 OCTOBER. Last he
 avy lower-body work is done.\n14 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
